Now the fix: bound loop by both lengths, and only return offer when i == len(accepted) && len(accepted) <= len(offer).

Careful with wildcard behavior: current code returns offer when accepted[i]=='*' or offer[i]=='*' at any position i where i < len(accepted) and i < len(offer). With the fix, the loop bound is min(len(accepted), len(offer)). If accepted is longer than offer, and the '*' occurs at position beyond len(offer), then it won't be reached. But if accepted is longer, then i can't reach len(accepted) so no match anyway. But wildcard check could trigger before... e.g. accepted="text/*x", offer="text/plain": i=5: accepted[5]='*' -> return offer. Hmm, that's existing behavior (wildcard at position 5 within both). Keep it.

